# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_cross_substrate_iac.py" "IAC-SUBSTRATE GATE: PASS" "IaC cross-substrate coupling: Terraform resource references + Kubernetes label-selector and configMapRef couplings, multi-definer false coupling suppressed" "iac-substrate: TF resource definition couples to cross-file reference (crown-jewel, no code edge); precision: comment-only type.name tokens do NOT couple (no definition = no mint); data sources: data.type.name cross-file coupling works; self-coupling: defining file gets alters only, not queries; content-free: resource values never appear in the graph; multi-definer precision: the same type.name DEFINED in two different module dirs does NOT couple (duplication, not a shared resource) while same-module def-to-reference still couples (recall); K8s label-selector coupling: Service to Deployment cross-file (same dir + same namespace only); K8s configMapRef coupling: Deployment to ConfigMap (same-dir locally-defined only); K8s namespace guard: no cross-namespace coupling; K8s multi-definer precision: the same kind/namespace/name defined by multiple files (cross-dir duplicate apps OR same-dir duplicate alternatives) does NOT couple, selector-to-labels def=1 within an app still couples; K8s precision: undefined resources not coupled; orchestrator integration: build_graph produces valid graph with iac_resource nodes; additive: pure-Python repo gets zero iac/k8s nodes (no regression)." "IaC cross-substrate: two .tf files that define/reference the same Terraform resource (type.name tuple) are coupled via an iac_resource node with NO code edge -- the crown-jewel coupling structural tools miss. Two-pass known-set discipline (mirrors _cg_schema): pass 1 collects locally-defined resource blocks; pass 2 scans for references to KNOWN names only (comment-only mentions or undefined names cannot mint). MULTI-DEFINER PRECISION (audit 2026-06-20, real repos): genuine shared-resource coupling is one definer to N referencers within a module; the same name DEFINED in multiple independent files is duplication, not a shared resource, and must not couple those definers. Terraform: the iac_resource node id is namespaced by the defining module DIRECTORY (a module = a dir), so aws_iam_role.this in module A and module B are different nodes (audit measured 64 to 18 pairs on terraform-aws-eks, 72 percent false removed) while main.tf and outputs.tf in one dir still couple. Kubernetes: the k8s_resource node is namespaced by the manifest DIRECTORY (one app = one dir) and a kind/namespace/name defined by more than one file in the same dir-scope (duplicate alternatives) is dropped from cross-file coupling; selector and configMapRef resolution is scoped to the same directory (audit measured 126 to 30 pairs on kubernetes/examples, 76 percent false removed) while same-app selector-to-labels and configMapRef def=1 patterns still couple. Content-free (resource names and file paths only, never resource values or Secret data). Never-crash (YAML parse errors and file read failures are silently bounded). Gate 127." 9
